  data: {
    LLM: 'Count outstanding tiles; aim to make layout totals that are multiples of 5. When leading, play a ten-point tile (5-5 or 4-6) if possible.\n\nBalance scoring, blocking, and playing to domino. Leave small totals for the next player to limit their scoring. Use information when an opponent draws (they lacked that pip).\n\nPursue scoring early when distribution is unknown; switch to blocking when you can count suits and force a blocked game with you holding fewest pips. Dominoing gives lead next hand.',
    Player: 'Count outstanding tiles; aim to make layout totals that are multiples of 5. When leading, play a ten-point tile (5-5 or 4-6) if possible.\n\nBalance scoring, blocking, and playing to domino. Leave small totals for the next player to limit their scoring. Use information when an opponent draws (they lacked that pip).\n\nPursue scoring early when distribution is unknown; switch to blocking when you can count suits and force a blocked game with you holding fewest pips. Dominoing gives lead next hand.',
